column73:
This should bypass it.  On the page, open up the console (right-click Inspect Element and go to Console tab) and type these 2 lines to remove 'to-build' class.  Then you can read through the slides without having to wait.<p><pre><code>  j = document.getElementsByClassName('to-build');
  for (k=0; k<6; k++) { for (i=0; i<j.length; i++ ) { j[i].className = j[i].className.replace(/ to-build /,'');  } }
</code></pre>
PS  I haven't done too much Javascript and someone else can probably write a shorter version, and I'm also not sure why looping just once isn't working.
